<title>UK: UK's Natl Power in Turkey power plant pact.</title>
<headline>UK's Natl Power in Turkey power plant pact.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British electricity generator National Power Plc said on Wednesday it signed a deal with its two partners to finance and build a 480 MW combined cycle gas turbine power plant in Turkey.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, National Power would take a one-third stake in the plant for $42 million, excluding associated costs, and would also operate and maintain it.</p>
<p>National Power's partners in the Marmara Ereglisi plant, with a one-third share each, included Japanese trading company Marubeni Corp, and Luxembourg investment firm Unit Investments SA.</p>
</text>
